10:T14af,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"Recipe","mainEntityOfPage":"https://crave.devyy.com/recipes/choc-chip-pecan-pie/","name":"Choc Chip Pecan Pie","image":["https://crave.devyy.com/ai-images/choc-chip-pecan-pie.jpg","https://crave.devyy.com/ai-images/choc-chip-pecan-pie.jpg"],"datePublished":"2026-11-01","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"@crave_testkitchen"},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Crave Recipes","url":"https://crave.devyy.com/","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://crave.devyy.com/icon-512.png","width":512,"height":512}},"description":"United States-inspired choc chip pecan pie with 12 measured ingredients — zero sign-up, instant Cook Mode. Ready in 45 mins (6 servings). 4.7★ rated with US/Metric scaling & hands-free Cook Mode.","prepTime":"PT15M","cookTime":"PT30M","totalTime":"PT45M","recipeYield":"6 servings","recipeCategory":"Pies, Tarts & Crumbles","recipeCuisine":"United States","keywords":"Choc Chip Pecan Pie, United States, Pies, Tarts & Crumbles, #ChocChip, #CraveMadeMeDoIt, #ViralDesserts, #UnitedSweets","nutrition":{"@type":"NutritionInformation","calories":"418 calories"},"aggregateRating":{"@type":"AggregateRating","ratingValue":4.7,"reviewCount":123},"recipeIngredient":["1.33 cup Plain Flour","5 tbsp Butter","6.7 tbsp Cream Cheese","1 tbsp Icing Sugar","10 tbsp Butter","0.83 cup Maple Syrup","1.11 cup Light Brown Soft Sugar","6.7 tbsp Dark Brown Soft Sugar","4 whole Eggs","1 tsp Vanilla Extract","1.78 cup Pecan Nuts","0.89 cup Dark Chocolate Chips"],"recipeInstructions":[{"@type":"HowToStep","name":"Dip & Coat Evenly","text":"First, make the pastry. Tip the ingredients into a food processor with 1 /4 tsp salt. Blend until the mixture resembles breadcrumbs. Drizzle 2-3 tsp cold water into the funnel while the blade is running – the mixture should start to clump together. Tip onto a work surface and bring together, kneading briefly into a ball. Pat into a disc, wrap in cling film, and chill for at least 20 mins. Heat oven to 200C/180C fan/gas 6. Incorporate 1.33 cup plain flour, 5 tbsp butter, 6.7 tbsp cream cheese, and 1 tbsp icing sugar smoothly until evenly distributed.","url":"https://crave.devyy.com/recipes/choc-chip-pecan-pie/#step-1"},{"@type":"HowToStep","name":"Shape & Press Dough Evenly","text":"Remove the pastry from the fridge and leave at room temperature for 5 mins to soften. Flour the work surface, then unwrap the pastry and roll to a circle the thickness of a £1 coin. Use the pastry to line a deep, 23cm round fluted tin – mine was about 3cm deep. Press the pastry into the corners and up the sides, making sure there are no gaps. Leave 1cm pastry overhanging (save some of the pastry scraps for later). Line with baking parchment (scrunch it up first to make it more pliable) and fill with baking beans. Blind-bake for 15-20 mins until the sides are set, then remove the parchment and beans and return to the oven for 5 mins until golden brown. Trim the pastry so it’s flush with the top of the tin – a small serrated knife is best for this. If there are any cracks, patch them up with the pastry scraps. Incorporate 10 tbsp butter, 0.83 cup maple syrup, 1.11 cup light brown soft sugar, 6.7 tbsp dark brown soft sugar, 4 whole eggs, 1 tsp vanilla extract, 1.78 cup pecan nuts, and 0.89 cup dark chocolate chips smoothly until evenly distributed.","url":"https://crave.devyy.com/recipes/choc-chip-pecan-pie/#step-2"},{"@type":"HowToStep","name":"Cream Butter & Sugar Fluffy","text":"Meanwhile, weigh the butter, syrup and sugars into a pan, and add 1 /4 tsp salt. Heat until the butter has melted and the sugar dissolved, stirring until smooth. Remove from the heat and cool for 10 mins. Reduce oven to 160C/140C fan/gas 3.","url":"https://crave.devyy.com/recipes/choc-chip-pecan-pie/#step-3"},{"@type":"HowToStep","name":"Cool, Garnish & Serve","text":"Beat the eggs in a bowl. Add the syrup mixture, vanilla and pecans, and mix until well combined. Pour half the mixture into the tart case, scatter over half the chocolate chips, then cover with the remaining filling and chocolate chips. Bake on the middle shelf for 50-55 mins until set. Remove from the oven and leave to cool, then chill for at least 2 hrs before serving.","url":"https://crave.devyy.com/recipes/choc-chip-pecan-pie/#step-4"}]},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://crave.devyy.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Pies, Tarts & Crumbles","item":"https://crave.devyy.com/category/pies-tarts/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"Choc Chip Pecan Pie","item":"https://crave.devyy.com/recipes/choc-chip-pecan-pie/"}]},{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does it take to make Choc Chip Pecan Pie?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Choc Chip Pecan Pie takes 45 minutes total (15 minutes prep) and yields 6 servings at 418 calories per serving."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I make Choc Chip Pecan Pie healthier or with zero refined sugar?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes! Toggle the Healthy Swap mode on this Choc Chip Pecan Pie recipe page to convert ingredients into lower-sugar, higher-protein, or wholesome alternatives automatically."}}]}]}5:[["$","script",null,{"id":"crave-recipe-jsonld","type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$10"}}],"$L11","$L12"]
15:I[2206,["882","static/chunks/882-23bd5690b5086ff1.js","178","static/chunks/app/recipes/%5Bslug%5D/page-ff1ba417b1c5ec11.js"],"App"]
13:T42c,Remove the pastry from the fridge and leave at room temperature for 5 mins to soften. Flour the work surface, then unwrap the pastry and roll to a circle the thickness of a £1 coin. Use the pastry to line a deep, 23cm round fluted tin – mine was about 3cm deep. Press the pastry into the corners and up the sides, making sure there are no gaps. Leave 1cm pastry overhanging (save some of the pastry scraps for later). Line with baking parchment (scrunch it up first to make it more pliable) and fill with baking beans. Blind-bake for 15-20 mins until the sides are set, then remove the parchment and beans and return to the oven for 5 mins until golden brown. Trim the pastry so it’s flush with the top of the tin – a small serrated knife is best for this. If there are any cracks, patch them up with the pastry scraps. Incorporate 10 tbsp butter, 0.83 cup maple syrup, 1.11 cup light brown soft sugar, 6.7 tbsp dark brown soft sugar, 4 whole eggs, 1 tsp vanilla extract, 1.78 cup pecan nuts, and 0.89 cup dark chocolate chips smoothly until evenly distributed.11:["$","noscript",null,{"children":["$","article",null,{"children":[["$","h1",null,{"children":"Choc Chip Pecan Pie"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"United States-inspired choc chip pecan pie with 12 measured ingredients — zero sign-up, instant Cook Mode. Ready in 45 mins (6 servings). 4.7★ rated with US/Metric scaling & hands-free Cook Mode."}],["$","h2",null,{"children":"Ingredients"}],["$","ul",null,{"children":[["$","li","0",{"children":"1.33 cup Plain Flour"}],["$","li","1",{"children":"5 tbsp Butter"}],["$","li","2",{"children":"6.7 tbsp Cream Cheese"}],["$","li","3",{"children":"1 tbsp Icing Sugar"}],["$","li","4",{"children":"10 tbsp Butter"}],["$","li","5",{"children":"0.83 cup Maple Syrup"}],["$","li","6",{"children":"1.11 cup Light Brown Soft Sugar"}],["$","li","7",{"children":"6.7 tbsp Dark Brown Soft Sugar"}],["$","li","8",{"children":"4 whole Eggs"}],["$","li","9",{"children":"1 tsp Vanilla Extract"}],["$","li","10",{"children":"1.78 cup Pecan Nuts"}],["$","li","11",{"children":"0.89 cup Dark Chocolate Chips"}]]}],["$","h2",null,{"children":"Step-by-Step Instructions"}],["$","ol",null,{"children":[["$","li","1",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Dip & Coat Evenly"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"First, make the pastry. Tip the ingredients into a food processor with 1 /4 tsp salt. Blend until the mixture resembles breadcrumbs. Drizzle 2-3 tsp cold water into the funnel while the blade is running – the mixture should start to clump together. Tip onto a work surface and bring together, kneading briefly into a ball. Pat into a disc, wrap in cling film, and chill for at least 20 mins. Heat oven to 200C/180C fan/gas 6. Incorporate 1.33 cup plain flour, 5 tbsp butter, 6.7 tbsp cream cheese, and 1 tbsp icing sugar smoothly until evenly distributed."}]]}],["$","li","2",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Shape & Press Dough Evenly"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"$13"}]]}],["$","li","3",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Cream Butter & Sugar Fluffy"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Meanwhile, weigh the butter, syrup and sugars into a pan, and add 1 /4 tsp salt. Heat until the butter has melted and the sugar dissolved, stirring until smooth. Remove from the heat and cool for 10 mins. Reduce oven to 160C/140C fan/gas 3."}]]}],["$","li","4",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Cool, Garnish & Serve"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Beat the eggs in a bowl. Add the syrup mixture, vanilla and pecans, and mix until well combined. Pour half the mixture into the tart case, scatter over half the chocolate chips, then cover with the remaining filling and chocolate chips. Bake on the middle shelf for 50-55 mins until set. Remove from the oven and leave to cool, then chill for at least 2 hrs before serving."}]]}]]}],"$L14"]}]}]
